[xUnit.net 00:00:39.31]       JOURNEY-GAP: the CONSUMER employee-ordering surface (payer strip, eligibility state, the CompanyAccount payment option, reduce-or-switch) is a separate consumer-app lane. The backend attribution seam it drives — quote → CartService.PromoteToOrder(CompanyAccount) bind → capture — is proven end-to-end in MealsPilotFullLoopJourneyTests and MealsOrderLoopJourneyTests.
[xUnit.net 00:00:39.31]       JOURNEY-GAP: the human-readable statement PDF export is a documented fast-follow (CSV ships, spec §13.3). The gap BOUNDARY is asserted green in MealsPilotFullLoopJourneyTests (a pdf request returns the typed meals.export-format-unsupported 400); the byte-deterministic PDF renderer is a later wave.
